  "base": {
    "contract": "atum.cloud-execution/1.10",
    "path": "spec/cloud-execution/v1.10",
    "sha256": "9d0ff12e2df9a10ecd93dcc142f62c737ff77c3a9a73965985f6aa01e6beb175",
    "rule": "additive: every 1.10 type, message, invariant and fixture is carried unchanged; 1.11 adds the per-agent daily-cap refusal, its cap and spend facts, and the cap-0 admission vector"
  },
  "row": "Reliability-first program item 23 (D25/S18): per-agent daily spending cap refusal",
  "amendments": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "sections": [
        "§6.1",
        "§9"
      ],
      "change": "a successfully dispatched turn or scheduled occurrence may remain live for at most 7,200,000 ms; the model grant never outlives that task and all existing stop, lease, funding and expiry fences remain"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "sections": [
        "§6.1",
        "§10"
      ],
      "change": "platform-route dispatch and its client fallback cover the same two-hour task window; the pre-dispatch claim remains short and replay-safe, and a lost dispatch response remains uncertain rather than retried"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "sections": [
        "§6.2"
      ],
      "change": "production computeSeconds may move from 1,800 to 7,200 only in the serialized money-policy operation; this contract does not change that row or authorize the switch"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "sections": [
        "§6.3"
      ],
      "change": "a managed dispatch carries one singleton alias, its logical model and effort, the immutable managed policy-map digest, exact context/output budgets and a max-turn hold no larger than the task ceiling; default source is alias default with logical model nguyet-thuc, while an explicit saved choice uses its named alias"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "the controller accepts every frozen managed alias instead of hard-coding default, admits exactly that singleton grant to the broker, applies the effort and per-alias budgets before the call, and never accepts provider endpoints, credentials, arbitrary reasoning objects or a cloud ChatGPT subscription"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "conversation compatibility includes the immutable policy-map digest, not selected alias or numeric budget; switching large to small compresses before the next call, switching back does not reseed or expand beyond the selected row"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "sections": [
        "§6.3",
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "for canonical Main with a ready account Google grant or durable latch, DA issues only the strict google-protected grant from turn start; saved H-M choice remains stored but inactive and clients surface google_protected_only; every other agent remains not_eligible until P-D12"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "the cloud sandbox accepts exactly ATUM_GOOGLE_FENCE_ROUTE, ATUM_GOOGLE_LATCHED, ATUM_GOOGLE_TOOLS_URL and ATUM_GOOGLE_TOOLS_TOKEN as optional Google entries; the access token is memory-only, refresh credentials never enter controller or sandbox, and a latched turn refuses broad egress tools"
    },
    {
      "id": "A10",
      "sections": [
        "§6.3"
      ],
      "change": "once policy 2026-10-17.1 is active the platform's managed dispatch carries managed_lineup_grant: one singleton alias from default, nguyet-thuc or nhat-thuc, its logical model, a low/medium/high effort, the policy-map digest 489e82bc…, the policy row's exact context and output budgets, and a max-turn hold no larger than the task ceiling. default is the unsaved-agent alias and carries nguyet-thuc's numbers. The 1.7 managed_model_grant (digest 53c77b31…, six rows) is not emitted for new dispatches"
    },
    {
      "id": "A11",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "which of the three aliases dispatch can reach is the platform's cloud_dispatch_policy row, a data setting. The controller accepts exactly the alias the grant names, admits the singleton grant to the broker, and applies per-alias window and effort limits itself; a controller window cap is at most the grant's contextBudget and never changes the grant, the catalogue or the digest"
    },
    {
      "id": "A12",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "supersedes 1.7 A6 for line-up grants: conversation compatibility is a fixed controller compatibility value that changes only when tools or the system prompt change, not the policy-map digest, so a catalogue revision never reseeds a conversation. Switching alias keeps one session identity; a switch to a smaller contextBudget compresses before the next call, and a switch back does not expand beyond the selected row"
    },
    {
      "id": "A13",
      "sections": [
        "§6.3",
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "a managed admission may be refused with managed.admission.refusal: state refused, reason daily_cap_exhausted, the agent's cap (dailyProtons at least 1, timeZone Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh, warningPercent 80, counts atum_billed_only) and the Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh day's spend (day, usedProtons). usedProtons is held plus settled Atum-billed spend, ceiled once to Protons; it is at least dailyProtons in every refusal. A call admitted before the cap was reached finishes and its full charge is recorded; later calls and later turns are refused. dailyProtons 0 means no cap and never appears in a refusal. The refusal is not stored: every admission re-reads the cap, so a raise admits the next call and a lower cap below spend refuses the next one. It clears at 00:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh of the next day or with a cap raise; no retry duration is carried. A refused occurrence skips with reason daily_cap; no other reason is valid in this message, and a refusal is never couldnt_confirm"
    },
    {
      "id": "A14",
      "sections": [
        "§6.4"
      ],
      "change": "wire mapping: the platform returns the refusal in its existing controller error envelope as HTTP 403 {error:'matrix_403',details:{reason:'daily_cap_exhausted',cap,spend}}; the Mac owner-managed edge returns {error:'daily_cap_exhausted',retryable:false,details:{reason,cap,spend}}. details is this pack's refusal without state, so consumers that know only {error,details.reason} keep working. The sandbox's provider error code is atum_daily_cap_exhausted. The refusal is terminal for that message and is never an uncertain outcome"
    }
  ],
